remarkable story about the band you know  them imagine dragons which has millions  of fans all around the world an  encounter with one fan in their early  years has had such a powerful grip on  them for nearly a decade now  jamie yukas joined the band to learn how  an unforgettable teenager helps spur an  invaluable mission it's part of our  series we call it a more perfect union  which aims to show that what unites us  as americans is far greater than what  divides us  [Music]  before their mega success  imagine dragons was hustling for  recognition in small clubs like la's  viper room  no it's the same i love it  the year was 2012. its time would become  imagine dragon's debut single  [Applause]  [Music]  the lyrics were influenced by dan  reynolds lifelong struggle with  depression and while the song introduced  the band to the world it touched the  very soul of a young fan we were a small  unsigned act there was a boy in the  audience that was a super fan that was  raised on his brother's shoulders who  had no hair because of chemo and was  skin and bones was really in the middle  of cancer that superfan was 16 year old  tyler robinson fighting stage 4 cancer  his brother jesse actually snuck tyler  out of the hospital to take him to see  his favorite band  i told him mom and dad are going to come  down on me hard  so you have to back me up if we're doing  this and he's like i got it i got it  we're doing this we did what we always  did we  stole my dad's car and just went  and listened to music jesse had sent the  group a facebook message asking them to  sing it's time for tyler explaining the  song has been his fighting theme through  chemo  that moment when their heads touch and  they're singing to each other screaming  at the top of their lungs  i'll never forget that moment ever as  long as i live i never felt any emotion  like that even felt incredibly spiritual  and going home it was like an amazing  thing to share with my family and it's  we didn't get in trouble  a friendship was born that night  and as the band began to catch fire dan  would text tyler to share the joy he was  just there to enjoy the music but his  attitude towards life was so inspiring  and i can honestly say from that moment  i have been changed  [Applause]  [Music]  the band dedicated their next single  demons to tyler the video has now been  viewed nearly 1 billion times but in  2013 the cancer returned and attacked  tyler's brain dan called me he had just  gotten some terrible news about tyler  and just was so distraught and we cried  together and  thought that tyler's legacy has to live  on  shortly after his death the band reached  out to tyler's parents about launching  the tyler robinson foundation  its mission helping families bear the  emotional and financial burden of  children fighting cancer i always  thought okay  good people care about their children  great people care about other people's  children that's unbelievable that  someone cares that much  this year's fundraiser in las vegas  brought in more than two and a half  million dollars there's nothing  that  grounds you quicker and reminds you  of what matters than when you see a kid  who is yet to get to experience all the  things that you have that has been given  a cancer diagnosis it's a diagnosis for  the whole family seeing the kids that  that we're able to help and everything  they go through it's the most meaningful  thing that we've been able to do  sorry  i'm appreciating that you're just being  as open as you are with your feelings if  i could hold it back i would  believe me whatever it  takes the non-profit has already  provided support to some 2 thousand  families  including eight-year-old jory bonners  what have they helped you with  rental assistance groceries christmas  it's been a big blessing  the family was on the verge of eviction  because jovi left his job to take his  son for treatments  now this tough little guy  is battling brain cancer again each time  it comes back it's just a little bit  more damaging for us because we know  time is not  on our side  [Music]  for the band the event is always an  emotional night  people have to drive meaning in a lot of  different ways i feel like that's one  thing that we know for a fact  we're making a difference we're doing  something powerful and important we love  you tyler wherever you are thank you for  all that you continue to share with us  you inspire us  reynolds was inspired to pledge a 50 000  donation if a guest was willing to sing  the band's huge hit  [Music]  12 year old cooper sandoval picked up  the mic and brought down the house  50 000 voice right there for cbs  mornings i'm jamie yukas in las vegas  radioactive indeed i've been following  imagine dragons since they first came  out and just when you think you couldn't  love them more there they go i love what  ben mckee said i mean he said if i could  hold it back i would don't hold it back  ben  i see you wrote down the same thing i  wrote down uh good people care about  their own kids yes great great people  care about other people's kids i wrote  that down too because i thought i want  to remember that that's true we should  all remember that that's for sure yeah  what a story all right thank you jamie  that's right
 

